@startuml
state client {
    [*] --> CLIENT_INFO
    CLIENT_INFO: 1. Take a information of single dir (a tuple) from database and send it;
    CLIENT_INFO: 2. Recv the reply from server.

    CLIENT_INFO --> [*] : if reply is DI_NO_NEED_DELIVER
    CLIENT_INFO --> SEND_FILES : if reply is DI_NEED_ALL
    CLIENT_INFO --> SEND_TUPLES: if reply is DI_NEED_COMPARE

    CLIENT_INFO --> SERVER_INFO: 1

    SEND_FILES: Send all files from dir
    SEND_FILES --> RECV_FILES
    SEND_FILES --> [*]

    note top of SEND_FILES
    use database to get all files path
    end note

    SEND_TUPLES: Send all tuples from a files table in database, where record the stat of files (the folder specified in this task)
    SEND_TUPLES --> CLIENT_FILES_NEED : after send all tuples
    SEND_TUPLES --> RECV_TUPLES_AND_COMPARE
    
    CLIENT_FILES_NEED: 1. Recv a filepath, as a node of file_need_list and push it into the list;
    CLIENT_FILES_NEED: 2. Send single file which specified by a node of file_need_list, pop the front of list.


    CLIENT_FILES_NEED --> [*]
    CLIENT_FILES_NEED --> SERVER_FILES_NEED : 2

}


state server {
    [*] --> SERVER_INFO
    SERVER_INFO: 1. Recv a information of a single dir from client;
    SERVER_INFO: 2. Compare the corresponding information of local database, send reply based on situation.
    SERVER_INFO --> CLIENT_INFO: 2
    SERVER_INFO --> RECV_FILES : if reply is DI_NEED_ALL
    SERVER_INFO --> RECV_TUPLES_AND_COMPARE: if reply is DI_NEED_COMPARE
    SERVER_INFO --> [*] : if reply is DI_NO_NEED_DELIVER

    note top of SERVER_INFO
    The Situation is:
        If There has already a tuple of this dir, compare two tuples:
            if modify time is mismatch, server should compare the files of this dir with client, but now just return a signal to client: DI_NEED_COMPARE;
            if modify time is match, return: DI_NO_NEED_DELIVER;
        If There not exist in database, it means server need all files of it, return: DI_NEED_ALL;
    end note


    RECV_FILES: Loop and recv single file until sending process of client is done
    RECV_FILES --> [*]

    RECV_TUPLES_AND_COMPARE: Compare the recv tuples with local database,
    RECV_TUPLES_AND_COMPARE: Store filepath as a node, add filepath to file_need_list
    RECV_TUPLES_AND_COMPARE --> SERVER_FILES_NEED

    SERVER_FILES_NEED: 1. Send only one node of file_need_list at a time (give client a filepath)
    SERVER_FILES_NEED: 2. After client remind, recv single file (Let the modoule 'recv_single_file' to handle it).
    SERVER_FILES_NEED --> [*]
    SERVER_FILES_NEED --> CLIENT_FILES_NEED : 1



}


@enduml
